DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("cos((x^2-3*x+1))");
$fun_1 = Formula("1*(ln((x/4)))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_3 = Compute("[3, 5] U (-infinity, 18)");
$set_ans_4 = Compute("([3, 5] - ([3, 5] U (((-infinity, 18) U (((-infinity, 18))) U ((-infinity, 18)) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (((-infinity, 18)) U [3, 5] - ((-infinity, infinity) - [3, 5]))))) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (-infinity, 18))))");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("([3, 5] - ([3, 5]))");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("[9, infinity) U (([9, infinity) - ((-infinity, infinity) - [9, infinity)))) U [9, infinity) - ((-infinity, infinity) - ({3, 4, 6}))");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("[9, infinity) - ((-infinity, infinity) - ({3, 4, 6})) - ((-infinity, infinity) - [9, infinity))");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

Lily was organizing her book collection. She had [`10`] shelves in her room, each with [`1`] book. Her parents bought her [`10`] new bookshelves, and each new shelf could hold [`19`] books. How many books can Lily store in total on all her shelves?

[_____]{200}
[%
10*1+10*19

First, calculate the book capacity of the original shelves: 10 × 1 = 10 books. Then, calculate the book capacity of the new shelves: 10 × 19 = 190 books. Finally, add both capacities together: 10 + 190 = 200 books.
%]
---

During a classroom activity, Emma collected [`8`] colorful paper stars from one table and [`17`] stars from another table. Her teacher then gave her a special sheet with [`10`] stars and told her to share them equally among [`10`] students, keeping one share for herself. How many stars does Emma have in total?

[_____]{26}
[%
8+17+10/10

First, calculate the stars from the special sheet: 10 ÷ 10 = 1 star. Then, add all the stars together: 8 + 17 + 1 = 26 stars.
%]
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{3, 4, 6\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x \geq 9\}`]

Compute:
- [`B \cup ((B \cap B)) \cup B \cap (A) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`B \cap (A) \cap B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | 3 \leq x \leq 5\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x < 18\}`]

Compute:
- [`A \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}
- [`A - (A \cup ((B \cup ((B)) \cup (B) \cap ((B) \cup A \cap A))) \cap B) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`A - (A) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 3, 8, 7 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 2, -8, 7 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<2, -8, 7>") x Compute("<3, 8, 7>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<2, -8, 7>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<2, -8, 7>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<3, 8, 7>"))}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<2, -8, 7>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<3, 8, 7>") . Compute("<2, -8, 7>")}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -1, -4, -8 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 8, 6, 8 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-1, -4, -8>"))}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<8, 6, 8>"))}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<8, 6, 8>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-1, -4, -8>") x Compute("<8, 6, 8>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-1, -4, -8>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-1, -4, -8>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f'(1) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>1)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}
- [`f'(1) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>1)}
- [`f'(7) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>7)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
